# **Proposition**
---

## Main Idea
Proposition is declarative sentence that declares a fact, it can be either true or false but not both.

My example:
  - Binary number system is the foundation of modern computing. (TRUE)
  - Linux is widely used worldwide, powering infrastructures. (TRUE)
  - All computers uses decimal number as foundation (FALSE)
  

Source:
Discrete Mathematics and Its Application (1.1.2 Proposition)
https://www.math.uh.edu/~irina/MATH3336/3336Notes/3336S11.pdf
